WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.180
Over the years, Jar Jar Binks has become emblematic
of the Star Wars prequel era — as well as

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.860
the totem the internet holds up to argue how
terrible those three films were.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.600
In the years following the release of The
Phantom Menace, fans denounced Jar Jar as

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.350
little more than a cheap money grab made to
sell toys… and that was at best.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:21.160
At worst, they described him as all the worst
aspects of Star Wars distilled into one character

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.759
— with some critics suggesting the character
represented a racist stereotype, on account

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.160
of his cartoonish accent.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:32.440
"No, no mesa stay. Mesa called Jar Jar Binks.  Mesa your servant."

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.500
At the center of all this, though, was the
man who portrayed Jar Jar: Ahmed Best.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.860
When he was cast for the first Star Wars movie
in in almost 20 years, Best was coming off

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.300
a celebrated turn in the hit musical Stomp
in San Francisco.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.300
And in 1997, Best went into production on
The Phantom Menace with bright eyes and a

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.340
cheerful attitude.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.000
It's easy to see how much fun he had behind
the scenes of The Phantom Menace, too: singing,

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.440
dancing, and chipper as ever, even when he
was draped in latex during a searing Tunisian

00:00:59.440 --> 00:00:59.940
summer.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.180
But that all changed in May 1999.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:06.680
Practically everybody who was around back
then was aware of the fan backlash against

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.220
the inclusion of Jar Jar Binks in Star Wars
canon.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.740
And in fairness, Best's overwrought Buster
Keaton impression didn't exactly fit well

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.920
into a film all about taxes and trade confrontations.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.280
Even so, however, it's easy to forget today
just how toxic that backlash became.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:25.619
A number of hate websites cropped up on the
internet, wishing all kinds of horrible things

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:26.580
upon the character.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.020
Even major news entertainment outlets ran
stories about the frothing hate against Jar

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.720
Jar that, over time, gradually became more
and more disturbing.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:39.500
Some Star Wars fans even led calls for Gungan
genocide; comments which were probably intended

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:43.700
to be humorous — but which nonetheless feel
particularly un-funny in this day and age.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.799
It's not that Jar Jar Binks was just unliked
or even hated — it's that so many people

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:52.590
relished the idea of exterminating something
that only existed as a fictional construct.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:57.029
To his credit, George Lucas warned Best ahead
of time that there might be anger in response

00:01:57.029 --> 00:02:00.549
to Jar Jar the same way there had been to
the Ewoks [EE-woks] in Return of the Jedi.

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:05.100
And for what it's worth, Lucas also publicly
defended Best when the backlash turned out

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.100
to be much, much worse than either of them
could have imagined.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.760
Sadly, however, people can only hold up against
so much public vilification for so long.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:17.620
After taking about as much as anyone can be
expected to take, Best became suicidal.

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:21.879
In July 2018, the actor revealed in a Twitter
post that he nearly decided to jump off a

00:02:21.879 --> 00:02:26.260
bridge due to the media backlash against Jar
Jar — a backlash that still affects his

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.220
career today.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.980
Several months later, he opened up in greater
detail about how the harassment he faced for

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.980
playing Jar Jar Binks pushed him to consider
suicide.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:39.660
"I just wanted to play a part. It was exhausting, you know."

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:44.500
Over the last 20 years, Star Wars fans have
had plenty of time to reflect on the successes

00:02:44.519 --> 00:02:46.099
and failures of the prequel movies.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:49.721
And for many of the people who were around
when The Phantom Menace was released, it's

00:02:49.721 --> 00:02:54.240
given them a chance to realize that Jar Jar
isn't exactly a treasonous crime against Star

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:54.740
Wars.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:59.299
With that reassessment came empathy — and
in the online responses to Best's confession,

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:02.980
many apologized for getting wrapped up in
the frenzied fever of Jar Jar hate.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:07.099
Fortunately, Best's bad experience with the
Star Wars universe hasn't put him off making

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.460
a long-overdue return.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:13.860
In 2020, Lucasfilm will debut Star Wars: Jedi
Temple Challenge, a kids' game show featuring

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:18.120
a range of physical challenges and contests
— and all of it will be hosted by Best himself.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.600
Still, though, it's lucky things turned out
so well.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:24.680
Sometimes it's easy to forget that the Star
Wars movies are made by people with real lives

00:03:24.689 --> 00:03:28.099
and feelings, performing their craft earnestly
in good faith.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.560
Best's story is proof that everyone would
be far better off if fans took that to heart.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.960
If you or anyone you know is having suicidal
thoughts, please call the National Suicide

00:03:36.969 --> 00:03:40.569
Prevention Lifeline at 1-800-273-TALK (8255).

